SUMMARY:The SWAP: Trade Notes. Make Connections
DESCRIPTION:Do you have study materials collecting dust? A study strategy that’s helped you succeed? Are you looking for an accountability partner or extra motivation on your licensure journey? \n\nJoin HNOMA for The Swap\, an interactive event designed to connect aspiring architects\, exam candidates\, and recently licensed professionals. Exchange study materials\, share test-taking strategies\, and build a supportive community of peers navigating the A.R.E. process.\n\nThe Houston Chapter of NOMA and LeaderFlow are partnering to host this two-part experience. The evening will begin with a fireside-style panel discussion moderated by LeaderFlow\, featuring professionals who will share insights\, lessons learned\, and practical advice from their licensure journeys. Attendees will then break into smaller groups for facilitated discussions\, providing an opportunity to ask questions\, exchange resources\, and connect with others at various stages of the A.R.E. process.\n\nWhether you’re exploring licensure for the first time\, actively studying for exams\, or recently licensed and looking to give back\, we encourage you to join us.\n\nThere’s something valuable for everyone at The Swap.\n\nPanelists\nShreya Patel\, Harrison Kornberg\nTim Uzoigwe\, Perkins & Will\nJaniece Williams\, Leaderflow\nJavier E. Guerrero\, Martinez Architects\nFallon Barrett\, City of Houston\n\nRegister here 
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/the-swap-trade-notes-make-connections/
LOCATION:Perkins & Will\, 1001 McKinney St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/The-Swap.webp
END:VEVENT
