SUMMARY:Optimizing the Building Enclosure Envelope CE Event
DESCRIPTION:Building Enclosure Council of Houston Presents: \nOptimizing the Building Enclosure Envelope \nGenerative Design Strategies for Early-Stage Architectural Performance \nPresenter: Joe Fong\, RA\, LEED AP \nDiscover how Autodesk Forma and Generative Design are transforming the architectural workflow from early concept to team collaboration. In this session\, you’ll learn how to rapidly generate performance-based building massings tailored to site constraints\, perform comprehensive site analyses early in the design phase\, and streamline team coordination. Step into a unified\, shared workspace where design options can be evaluated\, compared\, and refined in real time. \nAIA CE Credit: Pending Approval \nSchedule: \n\n4:30pm – Check-in\n5:00pm – Presentation\n\nAdditional Information: \n\nBeer & Wine Available\nParking is not included\nA minimum of 3 business days’ notice is required to receive a full refund if you need to cancel your reservation.\n\n  \nTHANK YOU TO OUR UNDERWRITER SPONSOR! 
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/bec-houston-lunch-learn-3/
LOCATION:Architecture Center Houston\, 902 Commerce St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United States
CATEGORIES:Building Enclosure Council Committee,Continuing Education
ORGANIZER;CN="Rhonda Lowe":MAILTO:rhonda@aiahouston.org
END:VEVENT
